WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.520
- We don't know who leaked the draft

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.030
of the Supreme Court opinion
that overturns Roe v. Wade

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.640
and Planned Parenthood v. Casey.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.950
Was it a clerk, a justice?

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.080
Well, either way, is
someone going to jail?

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.070
Well, the Supreme Court
operates in secret.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.710
Famously, they don't even allow cameras

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.540
or video recording during oral argument.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.810
But nothing the Supreme
Court does is classified,

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.540
and it doesn't appear that
there's any specific law

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.020
that makes the leak illegal,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.260
and leaks have happened in
the Supreme Court before.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:26.250
The Roe decision itself was
leaked before it was public,

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.040
as was the decision in Dred Scott.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:28.873
And there are a bunch of books

00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:30.150
from after the fact from insiders

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.470
and clerks like Eddie
Lazarus and Jeffrey Toobin.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.260
So Supreme Court leaks happen,
but they are pretty rare.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.580
This one might be the most public

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.480
and Justice Roberts' head is
certainly going to explode,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.130
but there may not be
any criminal liability

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.130
for someone who did it.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.090
So to paraphrase law
professor Steve Vladeck,

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.953
the leak is a story,
but it's not the story.

